# Code owners are requested for review automatically, and are required
# reviewers on protected branches. GitHub resolves ownership by LAST
# matching pattern in this file, so more specific rules must appear below
# more general ones to take priority.
#
# The codebase is split into four domain modules, one per contributor,
# mirrored on the API and web sides. Until the other three collaborators
# join, everything falls to the catch-all below (the lead). As each person
# is onboarded, uncomment their two lines and replace the placeholder with
# their real GitHub username.
#
# NOTE: these must be individual @usernames. @org/team handles do not
# resolve on a personal repository — only inside a GitHub Organization.

# Catch-all
*                                      @jpangala

# ── Domain modules (uncomment as collaborators join) ─────────────────────
# Identity & Access — User, Division, AuditLog
# /apps/api/src/modules/identity/       @username-a
# /apps/web/src/features/identity/      @username-a

# Members & Projects — Member, Project
# /apps/api/src/modules/members/        @username-b
# /apps/web/src/features/members/       @username-b

# Bookings & Assets — Booking, BookingRoom, BookingItem, Room, Item
# /apps/api/src/modules/bookings/       @username-c
# /apps/web/src/features/bookings/      @username-c

# Finance — FinanceCategory, IncomeEntry, ExpenseEntry, Budget
# /apps/api/src/modules/finance/        @username-d
# /apps/web/src/features/finance/       @username-d

